1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,342
Look at those two carts again.

2
00:00:02,362 --> 00:00:07,065
Cart A is thinking, I will cut the price
and sell more.

3
00:00:07,085 --> 00:00:11,001
Fine, if A is the only cart on the path.

4
00:00:11,021 --> 00:00:12,575
B is already there.

5
00:00:12,595 --> 00:00:14,937
Customers walk to the cheaper board.

6
00:00:14,957 --> 00:00:19,660
So when A sells more, those cups used to
stop at B.

7
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:21,152
Here is the idea.

8
00:00:21,172 --> 00:00:24,508
What one cart takes home that hour depends
on

9
00:00:24,527 --> 00:00:26,745
both prices, not just its own.

10
00:00:26,765 --> 00:00:27,863
Try a test.

11
00:00:27,883 --> 00:00:30,101
Pretend the other cart is gone.

12
00:00:30,121 --> 00:00:34,203
If what you take home does not change, you
are not

13
00:00:34,222 --> 00:00:35,694
in a game yet.

14
00:00:35,714 --> 00:00:39,050
You just have a shop on an empty path.

15
00:00:39,070 --> 00:00:40,868
Think of one cart first.

16
00:00:40,888 --> 00:00:44,141
Customers have nowhere else to buy, so
that cart

17
00:00:44,161 --> 00:00:46,687
can set a price and ignore everyone.

18
00:00:46,707 --> 00:00:49,232
On this path there are two carts.

19
00:00:49,252 --> 00:00:52,505
Customers look at both prices and walk to
the

20
00:00:52,525 --> 00:00:53,397
cheaper one.

21
00:00:53,417 --> 00:00:56,670
Each cart has to think about the other
board.

22
00:00:56,690 --> 00:00:57,735
Now watch B.

23
00:00:57,755 --> 00:01:00,576
A puts a lower price on the board.

24
00:01:00,596 --> 00:01:03,062
B leaves its price where it is.

25
00:01:03,082 --> 00:01:04,838
Customers walk over to A.

26
00:01:04,858 --> 00:01:08,744
B did not touch the board, and B still
takes home

27
00:01:08,764 --> 00:01:09,809
less that hour.

28
00:01:09,829 --> 00:01:12,650
That is all I need you to see.

29
00:01:12,670 --> 00:01:13,800
Use two checks.

30
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:17,248
Can I say what this cart takes home
without

31
00:01:17,268 --> 00:01:18,781
mentioning the other one?

32
00:01:18,801 --> 00:01:22,613
If the other board changes and this board
does not,

33
00:01:22,633 --> 00:01:25,295
does this cart still take home less?

34
00:01:25,315 --> 00:01:29,127
If both answers are no, you can ignore the
other

35
00:01:29,147 --> 00:01:30,004
cart.

36
00:01:30,024 --> 00:01:31,920
Next we name the players.

